      "hpi": "The longitudinal record includes renal transplant status and extended-release tacrolimus. Other outpatient products in the extract: 24 HR metoprolol succinate 100 MG Extended Release Oral Tablet; Hydrochlorothiazide 25 MG Oral Tablet; 24 HR tacrolimus 1 MG Extended Release Oral Tablet [Envarsus]; amLODIPine 2.5 MG Oral Tablet. A prior valganciclovir prophylaxis course, 900 MG once daily, is part of this scenario. It was not on the pre-admission medication list. Fever and fatigue for six days were new. There was no chronic febrile illness at baseline. The transplant and the immunosuppression are the predisposition. Rejection, drug toxicity, and ordinary gastroenteritis were still on the differential at arrival. Arrival creatinine was 0.9 mg/dL. The presentation was the symptom above, not a preassigned cytomegalovirus diagnosis.",
